1
00:00:00,325 --> 00:00:01,625
One checkout request.

2
00:00:01,762 --> 00:00:03,325
One point eight four seconds.

3
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,000
Somewhere, this got slow.

4
00:00:06,425 --> 00:00:07,250
Meet Lantern.

5
00:00:07,362 --> 00:00:08,725
See where the time goes.

6
00:00:11,225 --> 00:00:14,175
Lantern follows one request through every service.

7
00:00:14,275 --> 00:00:16,625
The gateway, checkout, then payments.

8
00:00:16,762 --> 00:00:18,325
Payments is where it waits.

9
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,175
Open the trace, and the time lines up.

10
00:00:22,338 --> 00:00:25,700
Payments spends more than a second on one database query.

11
00:00:27,092 --> 00:00:28,992
Lantern suggests an index.

12
00:00:29,142 --> 00:00:32,617
Add it, and checkout drops to about two hundred milliseconds.

13
00:00:34,092 --> 00:00:34,567
Lantern.

14
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:35,892
See where the time goes.

15
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:37,742
Private beta, next spring.

